TEXT:
Nursing Update
Neuro: Pt acted appropriately throughout the night, alert and oriented; MAE w/good strength; PERL; Vicoden for pain, pt nauseos w/dose so MS04 given @ 0330 for pain;
CV: Cont 1st deg AV block; Also Cont PVC's-4 gm MGS04 given, Then PVC's less frequent; BP stable throughout the night (see carevue flowsheet); On amio @ .3 mg/min; Skin cool, pulses weak but palpable; Cont dusky R third finger, sluggish refill; CO/CI WNL per bolus method; SV02 WNL-drops to low 50's w/activity (repositioning in bed); Pacer attached and off;
Resp: 4 l NC; Sats 98 or better; Lungs clear; Strong cough (dry); ABG WNL; MCT in place to suction no air leak noted;
GI: Hypoactive BS; Abd soft; Reported nausea a few times throughout night-seemed to follow PO vicoden; Reglan given x1 w/adequate effect; Clear liq overnight
Gu: Foley in place, urine output adequate throughout night-on Lasix [**Hospital1 **]
Endo: NO insulin coverage required
ID: Afebrile
Plan: Monitor hemodynamics, pulmonary care, activity as tolerates

Nursing Update-CSRU
Neuro: Alert and oriented; Reported hallucination once during night-saw flowers @ foot of bed, however cont to mentate appropriately during night; PERL; MAE w/adequate strength;
CV: Cont to have 1st deg AV block w/PVC's; BP stable throughout night; Skin cool, dry; Generalized edema; Pulses palpable; Cont Cyanotic R third finger;
Resp: 2 L NC; Sats 98 or better; Lungs clear; IS 500; Strong cough; Resps unlabored;
GI: Active BS, abd soft; Clear liquids overnight; Denies nausea
GU: Foley in place-urine output adequate-lasix [**Hospital1 **]-responded well to evening dose
Skin: Petechaie over anterior thighs-improving;
Pain: Dilaudid PO for pain-pt reports adequate relief;
Endo: BS 69 @ 0000-Juice given w/ BS improve to 121
Plan: Transfer to floor; Cont activity

CSRU Nursing Update 7a-3p
Neuro: Pt w/flat affect, oriented x3; MAE; PERL; No neuro deficits noted;
CV: Pt in sinus rhythm until, 1330 when she converted into afib-rate 70's; BP stable-see carevue flow sheet; PA line d/c'd today w/o complication-CO/CI/SVR WNL prior to d/c; pt edematous all over; Skin warm and dry, pulses palpable; Pacer off, attached, captures and senses as documented; Receiving 1 unit PRBC's for HCT 27.8
Resp: Pt on 3l NC; Drops 02 sats w/decreasing 02 NC; Lungs diminished, Uses IS 500-750; Resps NL; Sats 97%; PL & MCT to suction, negative air leak, draining serosang
GI: Hypoactive BS; Reglan given this am for nausea; Poor appetite, will only take clear liq;
GU: Foley in place, urine output adequate-on lasix TID
Endo: No insulin coverage needed
Pain: Dilaudid PO @ 1330 for sternal incisional pain;
Activity: OOB to chair
PLan: cont pulm toileting, cont activity, transfer to floor when ready

NPN 1900-0700

neuro:  responds appropriately non-verbally to most nurse inquiries;
     extremties remain weak, though purposeful movements with arms;
     slept much of the night despite q1 hr sxning; still reaches for
     lines and tubes at times, therefore soft restraints cont;

resp:  vent settings unchanged; suctioned at least Q1 hr for moderate
     amount whitish thick return;

c-v:  sbp 90-'s to low 100's; remains on Lasix gtt at 4 mg/hr with
     desired therapeutic effect;  remains on hep gtt for DVT;

gi:  tolerating o-g feeding; tiny amount ob- stool at beginning of
     shift;

skin:  mild redness at site of peri-area edema; received good hygiene
     care;  all line sites w/out s/s phlebitis or infiltration;

gu:  urine draining via foley cath, dilute appearing, clear;

endo:  receiving q4 hr fs, covered with riss prn;

id:  remains afebrile; remains on IV Abx;

social:  no calls from family this 12 hours;

assessment/plan:  cpap trial today; continue to diurese excess
    fluids; trach and peg on friday;

npn 7p-7a (see also carevue flownotes for objective data)

dx: hypercarbic resp failure
    COPD, obstructive sleep apnea

Resp:
failed extubation [**1-27**], re-intubated; extubated again [**1-29**] approx 17:00;
   pt doing well during the evening on 0.50 humidified face tent; attempted wean to nc at 6 l, pt de-sat'd to mid 80's, returned to 0.50 humid. face tent with return of O2 sats to low-mid 90's;
   over the night resp therapist put pt on nasal face mask ventilation, pt's O2 sat very labile, from mid 80's to hi 90's; litre flow adjusted frequently from 4-6 litres;
   pt's lung sounds coarse/wheezy; is now on po Prednisone instead of IV steroids for COPD exacerbation;
   pt receiving neb treatments as ordered; cough conjested sounding;

ID:
pt also remains on IV levoflox for COPD exac, and po fluconazole for oral thrush; also on IV flagyl for bacterial vaginosis; pt afebrile overnight;

endo/nutrition:
FS 95 at 22:00, no coverage needed;
anticipate start of soft NAS diet in a.m. if continues to do well;

c-v:
b/p mid 90's to low 100's this night; pt on sq heparin to prevent blood clots;

PLAN:
1) continue current plan of care
2) address pt needs
3) Full Code
4) a.m. labs

CSRU Nursing Update 7a-7p
Neuro: Pt sleepy, awakens easily to voice, MAE w/equal strength, PERL, speech clear, face symmetric;
CV: Pt tachycardic, w/rate up to 120's PO lopressor started and IV doses of Lopressor given to decrease rate; During AM, pt developed elevated ST segs on Lead II, III on EKG-cardiology consulted and saw pt-no interventions ordered, cardiology suggested possible pericarditis, R graft occlusion; BP stable, pt edematous all over; Skin warm and dry, bilat lower pulses palpable; Pacer hooked up to pt, but off; PA line d/c'd this AM-CO/CI WNL prior to d/c;
Resp: Pt extubated @ 8AM; Currently on 4 liters NC; Lungs cl, diminished @ bases; Sats 96-98%; Resps non-labored; MCT x3 to -20 cm SX, negative air leak, draining sm amt serosang; IS ~750
GI: Abd soft, ND, NT; Hypoactive BS; Emesis x1 this afternoon, scant bilious, reglan given, pt denies nausea able to eat some fruit, clears;
GU: Foley in place, diuresed w/IV lasix x1 today w/good result; Urine clear yellow;
Endo: Insulin gtt off, Glipizide restarted this evening; will cont to follow glucose;
Activity: OOB to chair, tol well;
Plan: Cont to monitor EKG, HR, BP; Pulmonary toileting, cont activity;

ccu nsg admit note.
(Continued)
). support family re:pt prognosis & dnr status.
